Figure 5, through flow cytometry dot plots (A) and histograms (B), demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A shows that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) and Nano-11 alone result in modest uptake by BMDCs, their combination (Nano-11+OVA) leads to a substantial increase in cells positive for both Nano-11 and OVA. Panel B further confirms this, illustrating a clear shift to higher fluorescence intensity for FITC-OVA when adsorbed to Nano-11, indicating increased antigen internalization compared to soluble OVA. These findings support Nano-11's role as an effective vaccine delivery vehicle.